<title>JAPAN: TABLE-Japan May household spending down 2.2 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Japan May household spending down 2.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's household spending in May fell 2.2 percent in real terms from a year earlier to an average 312,345 yen per household, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of year-on-year percentage</p>
<p>changes in May and April in real and nominal terms:</p>
<p>					   May		  April</p>
<p>				     Real   Nominal    Real   Nominal</p>
<p>Overall household spending   -2.2    -0.3     -1.0    +0.9</p>
<p>(average 312,345 yen)</p>
<p>Spending by wage earners     -1.5    +0.4     -1.1    +0.8</p>
<p>(average 330,446 yen)</p>
</text>
